{"id": "EUVD-2026-90918", "enisaUuid": "ba4480d1-e077-3a4b-b8d6-c41902d4052a", "description": "A flaw was found in Foreman. OS command injection vulnerabilities exist in the foreman-rake db:dump and db:import_dump tasks. The application fails to properly sanitize user-supplied input in the destination parameter (during backups) and the file parameter (during imports) before passing them to a Ruby system() call for execution. An attacker with permissions to execute foreman-rake (e.g., via a restricted sudo configuration) can append malicious shell commands to the provided file paths.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T16:22:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T06:12:05", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74503", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74504", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74505", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74506", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-12541", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2489970"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-12541", "GHSA-rcq3-9wpf-p347"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 1.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08a1855f-564b-3973-a24c-8938340ea6b7", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.18 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:3.16.0.25-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "19914ef5-81ce-31b0-8c6f-f40b7a90e950", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:3.12.0.23-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "4b8349e6-4f13-354b-b59d-9ee447fe4d3a", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.17 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:3.14.0.22-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "910bd72b-2db4-31cd-99b2-44a413ad1acb", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.19 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:3.18.0.14-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "e51aac4f-5e52-3daa